{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563177,"nonce":"kEYoYPwhPYgjpKg10YLOPNgiqqk=","title":"Host interface for framework adapters","message":"The layer a framework targets to render with blinc_ts: what a JSX runtime, a Vue custom renderer (createRenderer), a Svelte or Solid renderer, or a hand-written DSL calls to make and change the UI. blinc_ts has none today: an app builds LayoutNodes and replaces children whole (setChildren), and nothing takes element or property names.\n\n**Shape, after the DOM operations renderers already target**\n- Elements by tag (div, text, button, input, canvas, ... the built-in set ashui has), and text nodes.\n- insertBefore, append, remove, and moving a node within or between parents, each O(1) on the native tree, not a rebuild of the child list.\n- setProperty by CSS property name and value (through blinc_abi's property router; see the box-model issue), setAttribute, id and classList, so selectors match (blinc_abi 449ad47 for the cascade).\n- addEventListener and removeEventListener with capture, bubbling and passive (see the events issue).\n- Reading back: bounds after layout, the node at a point, focus.\n- Mounting a root into a window (NativeWindowHost.attachScene) and unmounting it, with the Scope that owns it.\n\n**Rules**\n- No dependency on the SDK's reactive graph: Vue and Solid bring their own. Binding a signal straight to a property, which skips the framework for each change, is an optional fast path.\n- Batched: property writes in one tick are coalesced and submitted together (d1a4fbe).\n- No knowledge of any framework inside the SDK.\n\n**Done when** two thin reference adapters, a JSX runtime and a Vue custom renderer, each render the same scene and pass the same snapshot and event tests, outside the SDK's src. Components and state machines stay in 5c5fdd5, built on this.","files":null}]}